For segCount=1, `glyphIdArrayLength = (length - 16 - 8*1)/2 = (28 - 24)/2 = 2`.

The `glyphIdArray` starts at byte offset `16 + 8*1 + 2 = 26`. So `glyphIdArray[0]` is at byte offset 26, `glyphIdArray[1]` is at byte offset 28.

The loop:
```cpp
unsigned int count = this->segCount;  // count = 1
if (count && this->startCount[count - 1] == 0xFFFFu)  // startCount[0] = 0, not 0xFFFF
  count--;
for (unsigned int i = 0; i < count; i++)  // i < 1, so i=0
{
  unsigned int rangeOffset = this->idRangeOffset[0];  // = 4
  if (rangeOffset == 0)  // false
  {
    ...
  }
  else
  {
    for (hb_codepoint_t codepoint = this->startCount[0];  // codepoint = 0
         codepoint <= this->endCount[0];  // 0 <= 0
         codepoint++)
    {
      unsigned int index = rangeOffset / 2 + (codepoint - this->startCount[0]) + i - this->segCount;
      // index = 4/2 + (0 - 0) + 0 - 1 = 2 - 1 = 1
      if (unlikely (index >= this->glyphIdArrayLength))  // 1 >= 2? No
        break;
      hb_codepoint_t gid = this->glyphIdArray[1];  // reads at byte offset 28
      ...
    }
  }
}
```

So `glyphIdArray[1]` is read at byte offset 28 within the subtable. The subtable is at offset 12 within the cmap blob. So absolute offset within cmap blob = 12 + 28 = 40. The cmap blob is 40 bytes. So reading 2 bytes at offset 40 reads 2 bytes past the end of the cmap blob.

But the cmap blob references the SFNT data. The SFNT is 68 bytes. The cmap table starts at offset 28 in the SFNT. So absolute offset in SFNT = 28 + 40 = 68. The SFNT is 68 bytes. So reading 2 bytes at offset 68 reads 2 bytes past the end of the SFNT.

